TEXT -64 -336 Left 3 A3  DAC step response and settling, client board model, rails stepped 30 V and 100 V
TEXT -64 -296 Left 2 0 -> +Istep at 100 us, +Istep -> -Istep at 600 us, 1 us edges, 1 kOhm. Istep stepped 2 mA (30 V bench twin) and 5 mA. Bench: generator square 0/2 V, 1 us edge, scope across RLOAD.
TEXT 1488 -128 Left 2 Board net names
TEXT 1488 -96 Left 1 VCCP = VCC+     VCCN = VCC-     (LTspice names avoid + and -)
TEXT 1488 -72 Left 1 VP = V+   VN = V-   (floating supply for U1/U2, about +/-10 V around OUT)
TEXT 1488 -48 Left 1 OUT = U2 pin 6     REF = U2 pins 1+5, U1 pin 6     LOAD = J1 electrode,  GND = J2
TEXT 1488 0 Left 2 Check on the real board
TEXT 1488 32 Left 1 Q2 (top) must be NPN MJD340, Q1 (bottom) PNP MJD350.
TEXT 1488 56 Left 1 BOM swap (PNP on top) puts ~200 V across U1/U2 in sim: read the DPAK markings. See README.
TEXT 1488 88 Left 1 D3/D4: BZX84 confirmed; BZX84C5V1 (5.1 V grade) modelled.
TEXT 1488 112 Left 1 The clamp soft-limits INPUT near +/-5.4 V, so commands above ~5 mA compress.
TEXT 1488 144 Left 1 Not on the board: Rsrc (generator 50 ohm), RLOAD (electrodes / phantom).
TEXT 1488 168 Left 1 F1/F2 modelled as 0.5 ohm. C2/C3 ideal (no ESR).
TEXT 1488 200 Left 2 Model findings to confirm on the bench
TEXT 1488 232 Left 1 RL <= ~1k: TI's models rang at ~1 MHz; the G models do not (no PSRR modelled). Scope LOAD at RL = 1k.
TEXT 1488 256 Left 1 Proven in sim (README Step 2): 5 mA holds to ~14k; 10 mA never reached (clamp 8.3 mA, compliance 6.8 mA at 10k).
TEXT -32 464 Right 1 function generator, not on board
TEXT 1488 424 Left 1 RLOAD = phantom between J1 (LOAD) and J2 (GND)
TEXT 1440 568 Left 1 U1 buffers LOAD onto REF
TEXT -64 896 Left 2 !.include ../../model/client-board-models.lib
TEXT -64 936 Left 2 !.param RL=1k Istep=2m
TEXT -64 976 Left 2 !.step param Vrail list 30 100
TEXT -64 1016 Left 2 !.step param Istep list 2m 5m
TEXT -64 1056 Left 2 !.tran 0 1.2m 0 20n
TEXT -64 1096 Left 2 !.meas tran Ifin AVG I(RLOAD) FROM 300u TO 500u
TEXT -64 1136 Left 2 !.meas tran Ipk MAX I(RLOAD) FROM 100u TO 300u
TEXT -64 1176 Left 2 !.meas tran OS_pct PARAM (Ipk-Ifin)/Ifin*100
TEXT -64 1216 Left 2 !.meas tran t_enter_1pct FIND time WHEN I(RLOAD)=0.99*Istep RISE=1 TD=100u
TEXT -64 1256 Left 2 !.meas tran t_last_above FIND time WHEN I(RLOAD)=1.01*Istep FALL=1 TD=100u
TEXT -64 1296 Left 2 !.meas tran tset_us_approx PARAM (t_last_above-101u)*1e6
TEXT 720 896 Left 1 Acceptance A3 (archive step 3). Four runs, log order: 30V/2m, 100V/2m, 30V/5m, 100V/5m. Overshoot is stated vs final value, not vs the full swing. 30V/5m clips (A1); ignore its settling numbers.
TEXT 720 924 Left 1 tset_us_approx = last exit from the +1 % band on the rising step; if the current never exceeds 1.01*Istep that measure fails (harmless) and t_enter_1pct is the settling time.
TEXT 720 952 Left 1 Confirm on the plot (zoom 98-115 us) that nothing re-enters the band later. Plot: I(RLOAD) and V(INPUT)/1k.
TEXT 720 980 Left 1 Bench edge rate matters: do not infer damping from a 1 us edge the DAC will never produce.
